# References

## Current rebuild

- [[structured-observations-preserve-legal-state-and-order|Structured observation rebuild]] — Native fields and caller buffers match the frozen 512-state pinned-reference oracle bitwise over 8,176 offsets and pass the real Task 2.1 schema. Seeded states use Claude's R1 policy correction, v2. Verification round 1 fixes retire the grammar bridge to root and CUDA-guard pinned cases; branch `just prepare`: 254 Rust, 69 engine, 1,437 Python passed; merged with the trainer lanes: 254, 69, 1,618. Optimized timing is a pod handoff.
- [[kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe|Kaggriculture configs follow Isaiah's scaling_6m recipe]] — Task 3.4: 2-rank 128/8 and 4-rank 64/4 configs deliberately keep scaling_6m's global batch, optimizer, PPO, teacher and compile settings; they load through the real FullConfig with a typed KaggricultureEnvConfig; run_ppo startup checks every forward against the model's GEMM chunking before allocation, prints bounded headroom, then stops explicitly because no Kaggriculture env is wired yet.
- [[kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic|Kaggriculture model joins Isaiah's factory, trunk compile and masked critic]]: Task 3.1 model side puts the model in `ModelConfig` and `create_model` with game-checked specs. It dispatches trunk compile through a nominal `TrunkCompileAPI`, which compiles only the blocks behind `_run_trunk`'s guard, and it masks the winner softmax as Isaiah does. CPU tests only, Codex r1 found no functional defect; `FullConfig` now pairs it with the Task 3.4 `KaggricultureEnvConfig`.
- [[evaluation-and-truncation-follow-the-kaggriculture-objective|Evaluation and truncation follow the Kaggriculture objective]] — Tasks 3.2/3.3: raw-bank evaluation winners, economic reward kept on truncation, joint per-player clipping and value-mode guards, a per-evaluation seed in a checked int64 band (distinct per step within a run, not a global stream separator) and promotion telemetry logged after promotion completes; proven on the trainer seam (CPU TDD, fake env, 1,344 Python passes); since the Task 3.4 merge the guards run through the registered Kaggriculture env config and every `configs/kaggriculture*.yaml`; native env and a real Kaggriculture run pending.
- [[live-differential-parity-checks-the-rust-kernel|Live differential parity checks the Rust kernel]] — Task 1.1b generates traces from Kaggle's hash-pinned engine; 8 committed games and a 40-game sweep agree with Rust; 303 probes find two malformed-input divergence classes (Unicode digits, unhashable items), kept as minimal expected failures and classified only from their observed mismatch.
